From ace608eb97d9168218e2790468657439ed43bb29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <78512247+nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:10:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l35: return -ENOTSUPP for unsupported sysclk

The APQ8016/MSM8953 machine driver (apq8016_sbc) walks every codec on a
DAI link and calls snd_soc_component_set_sysclk() with the board's
shared digital-codec MCLK (9.6 MHz on MSM8953). It treats any error
other than -ENOTSUPP as fatal to link->init, which aborts the whole
sound card. When a CS35L35 shares such a card (e.g. Meizu M6 Note
(m1721), where the amp sits on its own MI2S link while the WCD internal
codec drives the headphone/earpiece path), the amp being offered a
frequency outside its supported reference list must not tear down the
working WCD path.

Return -ENOTSUPP instead of -EINVAL for an unsupported clock frequency
so a machine driver can gracefully skip the amp on this link and keep
the rest of the card alive. The frequency is genuinely unsupported (not
a bad argument), so -ENOTSUPP is the correct errno.

Signed-off-by: nomorecoolnicknames <78512247+nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l35.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l35.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l35.c
index 7a01b1d9f..d5560ea37 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l35.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l35.c
@@ -743,7 +743,7 @@ static int cs35l35_component_set_sysclk(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 		break;
 	default:
 		dev_err(component->dev, "Invalid CLK Frequency Input : %d\n", freq);
-		return -EINVAL;
+		return -ENOTSUPP;
 	}
 
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(cs35l35->regmap, CS35L35_CLK_CTL1,
-- 
2.39.5

